const itemRows=[['key','Buried Garden Key','The old key to Lilias’s garden, buried after the door was locked and uncovered in newly turned earth.','key'],['skipping-rope','Skipping Rope','A gift from Mrs Sowerby that gives Mary exercise, rhythm, and a reason to remain outdoors.','toy'],['gardening-tools','Child-Sized Gardening Tools','Dickon’s small spade, rake, and trowel allow Mary to clear weeds without damaging dormant growth.','tool'],['seed-packets','Flower and Vegetable Seeds','Packets selected with Dickon for planting, exchange, and the careful renewal of bare ground.','plant'],['wheelchair','Colin’s Wheelchair','The chair first carries Colin into the garden while his growing strength remains secret from the household.','vehicle'],['portrait','Lilias Craven’s Portrait','A curtained portrait reveals Colin’s resemblance to the mother whose death shaped both house and garden.','artwork'],['letter','Susan Sowerby’s Letter','A plain letter urges Archibald Craven to return home when the children’s work has made reunion possible.','document'],['garden-book','Illustrated Garden Book','A volume used by Mary and Colin to name flowers, imagine beds, and plan what the hidden garden might become.','book']]
